<!--
  Undock: stand up from the dock, switch the gait to MPC, back straight out
  to the staging pose with the controller's DockToPose (controller_id
  "Undocking"), then return to RL locomotion. Selected per goal by
  NavigateToGoal.behavior_tree ("undock.xml" or the absolute share path).
  The goal's `pose` is the DOCK pose, the same pose dock.xml was sent -- not
  the staging pose: this tree derives where to back out to with
  ComputeStagingPose, so the backend sends one pose for both trees.

  Starting state: the robot is LYING on the dock (dock.xml ends with a
  lie-down since 2026-10-14), so the first step is SetMotionKey key="0"
  (stand). A robot left standing -- a dock whose lie-down was refused -- is
  fine too: stand is then a no-op.
  Then key="5" (MPC) for the slow, precise walk, exactly as dock.xml.

  Why not a plain MOVE off the dock: the robot's footprint sits on the
  dock's lethal cells in the local costmap, so MPPI (the FollowPath
  controller) starts in collision and cannot be relied on to get off it; a
  mode switch and a navigation would also be two steps the backend has to
  sequence. The back-out is blind, like the approach -- the docking
  controller reads no costmap -- which is the point.

  Why backward rather than turning on the dock: the charging contacts are
  under the robot, an in-place turn on them is wear nobody has measured, and
  the space beside the dock is unknown; backing out along the line it came
  in on is the one motion known to be clear (opennav_docking undocks the
  same way). The Undocking controller instance reverses by itself when the
  target is behind it (allow_backward, no initial rotation), and its final
  rotation leaves the robot facing the dock at the staging pose, so the MOVE
  that follows starts from a known heading.

  The two Waits are guesses: 4000 ms for standing up, 1500 ms for the gait
  transition into MPC. Neither can be verified today -- SetMotionKey is a
  one-way UDP datagram with no acknowledgement, and the gait controller's
  reported mode (the `mode` topic, data[1]) has no known value for MPC. Once
  that code and the stand-up time have been read off the robot, both Waits
  become WaitForMotionState nodes in the same positions. A Wait too short
  switches modes mid stand-up or starts the back-out mid transition; do not
  shorten them without the measurement.

  Gait on exit: RL (key="1") on success, since a MOVE follows -- unlike
  dock.xml, which ends lying down on the dock and never switches back. On any failure after the MPC switch was attempted the Fallback's
  second child restores RL as well; a failure of the stand-up itself (the
  driver's safety lock, "LOCKED") fails before the gait was touched and needs
  no restore -- the robot is still lying down. A CANCEL during the back-out
  halts the tree without the restore, leaving MPC on with the robot standing
  somewhere between the dock and the staging pose; re-sending this goal
  continues from there (the staging pose is still behind the robot), or the
  backend restores RL itself.

  Attribution and status sentences follow dock.xml: SetMotionKey and
  DockToPose write themselves on failure and the navigator maps them to
  DOCK_FAILED (the DockToPose message says back-out, not approach);
  SetBlackboard writes the tree's own sentences ("Standing up", "Switching
  the gait to MPC for undocking"), DockToPose writes "Backing out of the
  dock", "Undocking: 0.42 m to the staging pose", "Undocked". There is no
  path, so the navigator's distance_remaining reads 0 throughout; progress is
  in status_msg.
-->
<root main_tree_to_execute="MainTree">
  <BehaviorTree ID="MainTree">
    <Sequence name="Undock">
      <SetBlackboard output_key="nav_status_msg" value="Standing up"/>
      <SetMotionKey key="0" server_timeout="500"/>
      <!-- Stand-up time: a guess until measured (header) -->
      <Wait msec="4000"/>
      <Fallback name="UndockInMpc">
        <Sequence name="SwitchAndBackOut">
          <SetBlackboard output_key="nav_status_msg" value="Switching the gait to MPC for undocking"/>
          <SetMotionKey key="5" server_timeout="500"/>
          <!-- Stand-in for a WaitForMotionState check; the value is a guess (header) -->
          <Wait msec="1500"/>
          <ComputeStagingPose dock_pose="{goal}" distance="1.0" staging_pose="{staging_pose}"/>
          <DockToPose dock_pose="{staging_pose}" controller_id="Undocking" goal_checker_id="dock_goal_checker" timeout="60.0"/>
          <SetMotionKey name="BackToRL" key="1" server_timeout="500"/>
        </Sequence>
        <ForceFailure>
          <SetMotionKey name="RestoreRL" key="1" server_timeout="500"/>
        </ForceFailure>
      </Fallback>
    </Sequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
